  "recent_hooks": [
    "The argument that tech stocks are cheap hinges entirely on believing the AI revolution is far from over. If Nvidia ($NVDA) handles its leadership transition and political headwinds soften, pulling back from this tech bear market might end up looking like the single best entry point of the decade.",
    "Michael Burry is trimming his downside bets, selling off 50% of his puts in both VanEck Semiconductor ETF ($SMH) and Nvidia ($NVDA), alongside 30% of his Zoetis ($ZTS) calls.",
    "Five years of crypto cycles and Bitcoin ($BTC) sits at $59,000 compared to $59,700 in November 2021, but the rest of the market tells a much harsher story. Ethereum ($ETH) is at $1,620 down from $4,410, Solana ($SOL) dropped from $220 to $69, BNB ($BNB) slid from $605 to $540, and XRP ($XRP) moved from $1.10 to $0.90. Holding anything outside the market leader over this stretch meant paying a massive premium for zero long-term progress.",
    "Citi, PNC, and Citizens changed their bank terms this week, and the fine print is brutal for anyone handing their credentials to ChatGPT or Claude. If you give an external AI agent your login and it empties your account, gets hacked, or ignores your instructions, the banks now count every transaction as if you personally authorized it. Zero refund. You are fully on the hook for whatever the bot does.",
    "Anthropic ($ANTH) is sitting on a record $237 billion cash pile after raising $81 billion in its IPO and another $26 billion in a private placement.",
    "Russia is officially letting its exchanges launch cryptocurrency trading, provided they clear it with the Central Bank. Going from a strict domestic crackdown to regulated exchange access shows how fast nation-states are rewriting their financial rules when global settlement needs change.",
    "US Treasury Secretary Bessent told CBS that committees are swiftly seeking answers on which level of Nvidia ($NVDA) business was aware. When the Treasury gets involved, a corporate investigation stops being an internal matter and becomes a sovereign risk calculation for the entire semiconductor supply chain. #nvidia",
    "The 3x leveraged long Semiconductor ETF ($SOXL) has erased 90% of its value since its June peak, dragging the fund to its lowest level since September 2025.",
    "Short sellers took an $11,300,000,000 loss on Nvidia ($NVDA) in a single day. Betting against the leader of the hardware cycle continues to be the most expensive position on the market. #nvidia",
    "-20 tonnes. That is how much global physical gold-backed ETFs lost last week, marking their largest weekly withdrawal since June. Gold ETFs have now suffered outflows in 3 of the last 5 weeks, coming out to -30 tonnes net. SPDR Gold Shares ($GLD), the largest gold-backed ETF in the US, led the damage by shedding -10 tonnes on its own as total US outflows hit -12 tonnes. China and the UK followed behind. Everyone watched gold hit highs while the underlying fund redemptions quietly started weeks ago.",
    "Bill Ackman analyzed 22,000 lines of Bernie Sanders campaign expenditures since 2017, totaling $53 MILLION spent.",
    "Gold under $3,470, the S&P 500 under 7,000, Nasdaq under 22,800, and Bitcoin ($BTC) under $58,000 all at the same time. Trillions in combined market value wiped out today because when liquidity vanishes, even the safe havens get sold to cover the rest.",
    "President Trump is blaming stock market weakness directly on recent midterm election wins by Democrats, arguing that the market and 401-ks would be BOOMING instead if he had been on the ballot.",
    "$600 million in stolen crypto from Binance ($BNB) has now been funneled through THORChain ($RUNE) by North Korean hackers. That is a massive volume of illicit capital moving right through a decentralized protocol in broad daylight, showing once again how hard it is to stop capital flows on-chain after a major exploit.",
    "Indian 10-Year Government Bond Yield Climbs to 7.2575% After Previous Close at 7.2365%"
  ],
